== the configuration, read from the standard input
account: mailto:ops@certs.test, the CA's terms agreed to
certificate site: certs.test, www.certs.test, 127.0.0.1, proved by http-01
certificate wild: *.certs.test, proved by dns-01
renewal: once 30 days or fewer are left, or once the CA's renewal window opens
keys: kept in the system's keyring
== the stand-ins, started on 127.0.0.1
dns: ready, the authority of certs.test, taking updates signed with the TSIG key certs-update
http-01 responder: ready, serving the webroot
acme: ready, the root of its own HTTPS handed to the client
acme: its issuing root fetched from /roots/0: CN=Certs Stand-in Root X1,O=Certs Stand-in CA
the configuration pointed at the stand-ins and the demo's folder, edited in place, its other lines kept
== day 0
account: made, its key made and kept, valid, contact mailto:ops@certs.test
account: the same key asked again finds the same account, none made: true
  certs.test: http-01, the answer served from the webroot at /.well-known/acme-challenge/<token>, fetched and found by the CA: valid
  www.certs.test: http-01, the answer served from the webroot at /.well-known/acme-challenge/<token>, fetched and found by the CA: valid
  127.0.0.1: http-01, the answer served from the webroot at /.well-known/acme-challenge/<token>, fetched and found by the CA: valid
site: version 1 kept, serial 14b8e6bf55221250efc60762dd43bdc2, issued by Certs Stand-in Issuer R1, valid 90 days, 89 days left
  *.certs.test: dns-01, TXT _acme-challenge.certs.test published by an update signed with TSIG, seen by the CA, then withdrawn: valid
wild: version 1 kept, serial 2c24411fe71145eb4c6c18de17dc4daf, issued by Certs Stand-in Issuer R1, valid 90 days, 89 days left
== what the stand-ins refuse, as a CA and an authority must
the same signed request sent twice: answered 200, then refused 400 badNonce
a request whose payload was changed after signing: refused 400 malformed
an update signed with a secret the authority does not hold: refused, the authority answered NOTAUTH
an update with no signature: refused, the authority answered REFUSED
other.certs.test, whose CAA names another CA: refused, the authorization of other.certs.test turned invalid: http-01: the CAA records of other.certs.test let no CA named standin.certs.test issue
www.certs.test, answered with another account's key authorization: refused, the authorization of www.certs.test turned invalid: http-01: the HTTP-01 answer of www.certs.test is not this account's key authorization for its token
an order for example.org: refused, the server answered 400 rejectedIdentifier: this stand-in issues for names under certs.test alone, not example.org
